--- body ---
## Context

Author, 2026-09-06: wants multilingual EN/FR/ES/VN, extensible. Every
user-facing string in the current sitter is hard-coded French.

## Design

- **Mechanism: Fluent `.ftl`**, the Zotero 7+/Firefox convention --
  `locale/<lang>/sdt-pack-sitter.ftl`, registered from `bootstrap.js` via
  `Localization`/`document.l10n`. Reasons over a plain JSON dictionary:
  plurals differ across all four target languages, and Vietnamese has no
  plural inflection at all -- Fluent handles this per locale without
  touching code. Dates and durations format through `Intl` per locale,
  replacing the current hard-coded `fr-FR`.
- **Extensible as data, not code.** A locale is a directory listing --
  adding a fifth language later is one `.ftl` file plus one manifest line.
  Fallback chain: requested locale -> its language without region -> `en`,
  the source of truth every string id must exist in.
- **Language selection** follows Zotero's own UI locale; no separate
  in-plugin setting.

## Sequencing note -- open question for the author

The plugin is still labeled "(experimental)" in its own manifest, and a
separate proposal is pending on whether its permanent home should move out
of this workshop repo into its own repository (mirroring zoteus). Building
a full Fluent pipeline here, then re-wiring it after an extraction, is
strictly more work than doing it once in the eventual home. This ticket
can proceed regardless -- the `.ftl` files travel with a `git mv` either
way -- but flag the sequencing choice to the author rather than assuming
"build it now" is free.

## Acceptance

- [ ] All four locales (en, fr, es, vi) complete for every string in the
      primary and details dialog layers (see 0693); the diagnostics layer
      may stay English.
- [ ] A missing-id fallback test, run with a deliberately truncated
      `fr.ftl`, shows English text where the id is missing and raises no
      exception.
- [ ] No locale literal (e.g. `'fr-FR'`) remains in code -- grep test.
- [ ] Wording from 0691 lands first; this ticket externalizes it, it does
      not also change it.
